{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_1186253214#6_2446339833","relevance":2,"reason":"The document provides direct evidence that the ACA excludes undocumented immigrants from marketplace subsidies and Medicaid expansion, but it is primarily about the remaining uninsured rather than dedicated to whether undocumented immigrants get free healthcare.","learned":"Undocumented immigrants are excluded from ACA marketplace subsidies and Medicaid expansion; they may buy individual-market coverage outside marketplaces."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"undocumented immigrants\" \"health coverage\" \"health care\" \"emergency medicaid\")","reason":"Look for dedicated explainers on health coverage and care for undocumented immigrants, including emergency Medicaid and access to care."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"undocumented immigrants\" \"health coverage\" \"health care\" \"emergency medicaid\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_759029027#2_1366945063","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1362","rank":1,"snippet":"receive federal funding to provide nonemergency coverage to these populations without a waiting period. Does this CHIPRA option provide benefits to undocumented immigrants? No. Undocumented immigrants remain ineligible for federally funded nonemergency Medicaid and CHIP. The new CHIPRA option did not change eligibility rules for <cover>undocumented immigrants. Remember, however, that eligibility rules apply only to individuals seeking benefits, not to the entire household. Thus if a lawfully residing child is eligible for Medicaid or CHIP as a result of this CHIPRA option, the child’s parents may apply for Medicaid or CHIP for their child, regardless of their own immigration status. Noncitizens whose immigration status renders them ineligible for nonemergency Medicaid are still eligible for emergency Medicaid. Thus, low-income, lawfully residing children and pregnant women may be eligible only for emergency Medicaid unless a state elects this CHIPRA option to provide them cost-effective, preventative coverage.\" , \"start_char\": 1771.000000 , \"title\": \"Federal Funding for States to Provide Health Coverage - National Immigration Law Center\" , \"url\": \"https://www.nilc.org/issues/health-care/</cover>federal-funding-for-states-to-provide-health-coverage/\" }"}}
