{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"illegal immigrants\" \"undocumented immigrants\") (+ \"free healthcare\" \"free health care\" \"free medical care\") (+ eligible eligibility receive))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_29_1470538552#3_3380634633","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1364","rank":1,"snippet":"hits Biden on taxes, immigration in new ad \" , \"segment\": \"The Trump campaign ad released Tuesday calls Biden’s plan “the biggest tax increase in history,” showing a cost of $4 trillion. The Urban-Brookings Tax Policy Center released a paper earlier this year finding that Biden’s tax proposals would raise approximately $4 trillion over 10 years and lead to the largest tax increases for high-income people. The new ad also shows footage of Biden vowing “citizenship for 11 million undocumented folks.” ADVERTISEMENT “That means 11 million <cover>illegal immigrants competing for American jobs, eligible for free health care, </cover>Social Security and Medicare. America can’t afford Joe Biden,” the ad continues. RNC featuring Tim Scott in ad campaign attacking Biden agenda Biden to meet with key GOP senator Wednesday on infrastructure Biden has vowed to work with lawmakers if elected to provide “a roadmap to citizenship for nearly 11 million undocumented immigrants,” according to his website. The ad is set to be released in key battleground states of Florida, Arizona, North Carolina, Georgia and Wisconsin, Axios reported . The ad will run in Wisconsin through the Democratic National Convention, which is set to take "}}
