{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1653338202#1_3433222046","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from the dedicated KFF brief on health coverage and care for undocumented immigrants. It directly states undocumented immigrants often are uninsured, may get limited low-cost community health center care, must receive emergency screening/stabilization, and that some states/DC use state-only funds for certain Medicaid-like coverage regardless of status.","learned":"Federal coverage is generally unavailable to undocumented immigrants, but emergency care, limited community health center care, and some state-funded coverage for children/young adults are exceptions."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"undocumented immigrants\" \"emergency medicaid\" eligible \"federal law\")","reason":"Search specifically for dedicated documents explaining the Emergency Medicaid exception for undocumented immigrants under federal law, a key part of the answer to whether healthcare is free."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"undocumented immigrants\" \"emergency medicaid\" eligible \"federal law\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_901758286#0_1512535688","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1369","rank":1,"snippet":"State - Limited Medicaid Coverage for Undocumented Immigrants Print Email to friend Share Share this article Link to article Add to pool Remove from pool Views: 81002 Posted: 22 Jun, 2009 by -- Updated: 09 Mar, 2021 by Valerie Bogart (New York Legal Assistance Group) COVID-19 ALERT - See here . COVID-­19 lab testing, evaluation, and treatment are emergency services and will be reimbursed by NYS Medicaid for individuals who are <cover>undocumented immigrants eligible only for emergency Medicaid. NEWS UPDATE March 9, 2021 - The Trump Public Charge rule has been vacated after the Biden administration withdrew its appeal to the Supreme Court of an injunction issued by the Second Circuit and also withdrew appeal of a Seventh Circuit lawsuit. See more about this news and public charge here . EMERGENCY MEDICAID Federal law </cover>requires state Medicaid programs to provide Medicaid coverage for \"care and services are necessary for the treatment of an emergency medical condition\" to immigrants who do not meet the immigration requirements for full Medicaid. This would be immigrants who are not PRUCOL . They must “otherwise meet [] the eligibility requirements for medical assistance under the State plan.\"\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title"}}
