{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_901758286#0_1512535688","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to limited Medicaid coverage for undocumented immigrants and directly states that federal law requires state Medicaid programs to cover emergency medical conditions for immigrants who do not meet immigration requirements for full Medicaid, if they otherwise meet eligibility requirements.","learned":"Undocumented immigrants who are not eligible for full Medicaid may still qualify for Emergency Medicaid for necessary treatment of an emergency medical condition, subject to other Medicaid eligibility rules."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1369","reason":"The Emergency Medicaid query is highly focused and produced a direct grade-3 result; continue to find more evidence on the emergency-care exception for undocumented immigrants."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1369"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_901758286#1_1512537773","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1369","rank":2,"snippet":"\"Emergency Medicaid in New York State - Limited Medicaid Coverage for Undocumented Immigrants Emergency Medicaid in New York State - Limited Medicaid Coverage for <cover>Undocumented Immigrants EMERGENCY MEDICAID Which Services are Covered as an Emergency? \" , \"segment\": \"NEWS UPDATE March 9, 2021 - The Trump Public Charge rule has been vacated after the Biden administration withdrew its appeal to the Supreme Court of an injunction issued by the Second Circuit and also withdrew appeal of a Seventh Circuit lawsuit. See more about this news and public charge here . EMERGENCY MEDICAID Federal law requires state Medicaid programs to provide Medicaid coverage for \\\"care and services are necessary for the treatment of an emergency medical condition\\\" to immigrants who do not meet the immigration requirements for full Medicaid. This would be immigrants who are not PRUCOL . They must “otherwise meet [] the eligibility requirements for medical assistance under the State plan.\\\" 42 U.S.C. § 1396b (v) (2) (A)- (C) . To qualify for Emergency Medicaid, clients need to be residents of New York State, financially eligible </cover>for Medicaid (under applicable rules for the individual's category (MAGI/ NON-MAGI), and the condition requiring treatment needs to manifest itself by acute "}}
