{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ medicaid undocumented immigrants \"emergency medical condition\" \"otherwise eligible\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_369243229#0_704652408","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1370","rank":1,"snippet":"emergency medical condition? Undocumented Non-Citizen Temporary Non-Immigrant What is an emergency medical condition? What services do not meet the definition of an emergency medical condition? How long is Medicaid coverage for the treatment of an emergency medical condition? Authorization Period \" , \"segment\": \"Medicaid for the Treatment of an Emergency Medical Condition Fact Sheet Medicaid for the Treatment of an Emergency Medical Condition Fact Sheet What is Medicaid for the treatment of an emergency medical condition? <cover>Medicaid payment is provided for care and services necessary for the treatment of an emergency medical condition, to certain temporary non-immigrants (e.g., certain foreign students, visitors/tourists) who are otherwise eligible and undocumented </cover>non-citizens. An undocumented non-citizen must meet all eligibility requirements, including proof of identity, income, and State residency to be eligible for Medicaid coverage of an emergency medical condition. Temporary non-immigrants, who have been allowed to enter the United States temporarily for a specific purpose and for a specified period of time, do not have to meet the State residency requirement to receive coverage for the treatment of an emergency medical condition and are considered \"Where Found\" for District of Fiscal "}}
