{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_369243229#1_704655227","relevance":2,"reason":"This is another segment from the emergency Medicaid fact sheet. It is related and defines undocumented individuals, but the snippet is less direct about undocumented immigrants receiving Medicaid-funded emergency care than the prior segment, focusing more on temporary non-immigrants.","learned":"The fact sheet distinguishes undocumented non-citizens from temporary non-immigrants; emergency Medicaid coverage is limited and category-specific."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1370","reason":"The query is still focused on emergency Medicaid and undocumented immigrants and may yield additional direct sources or clearer passages."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1370"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_901758286#3_1512541939","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1370","rank":3,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_901758286#3_1512541939\" , \"end_char\": 4259.000000 , \"headings\": \"Emergency Medicaid in New York State - Limited Medicaid Coverage for Undocumented Immigrants Emergency Medicaid in New York State - Limited Medicaid Coverage for <cover>Undocumented Immigrants EMERGENCY MEDICAID Which Services are Covered as an Emergency? \" , \"segment\": \"See article for where to apply in NYC NYS directives are summarized below. In 2013, NYS eliminated the form physicians were previously required to fill out -- DOH-4471 form for the Certification of Treatment of an Emergency Medical Condition . ( revised in 2010) Immigrants need only submit the standard Medicaid application, and if they are found otherwise eligible, </cover>local districts are to issue a Client Benefit Identification Card and authorize coverage for a 12-month period, plus an additional 3-months if retroactive coverage is requested. For a claim to be paid, the physician must enter an emergency admission type in eMedNY. Standard spend down and renewal processes apply. NYS DOH GIS 13-MA-009 http://www.health.ny.gov/health_care/medicaid/publications/gis/13ma009.htm In January 2016, "}}
