{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_901758286#3_1512541939","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment from a document dedicated to Emergency Medicaid as limited Medicaid coverage for undocumented immigrants. It gives direct supporting evidence that immigrants who are otherwise eligible can apply through standard Medicaid processes and receive time-limited emergency-condition coverage/payment authorization.","learned":"Emergency Medicaid for undocumented immigrants is limited coverage tied to emergency medical conditions and other Medicaid eligibility rules, not general free healthcare."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\") (+ \"emergency room\" hospital emtala) (+ \"regardless of\" \"ability to pay\" \"immigration status\"))","reason":"Search for direct evidence on the emergency-room/EMTALA exception: hospitals must provide emergency screening and stabilization regardless of immigration status or ability to pay, which is central to whether undocumented immigrants get free healthcare."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\") (+ \"emergency room\" hospital emtala) (+ \"regardless of\" \"ability to pay\" \"immigration status\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_410409857#7_918101125","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1371","rank":1,"snippet":"Covered Under Obamacare? Is Medical Help for Illegal Immigrants Covered Under Obamacare? How the Affordable Care Act Treats Undocumented Immigrants Individual Mandate and Undocumented Immigrants Controversial Claims Obama Refutes Claims Continued Criticism \" , \"segment\": \"\\\"Starting in 2014, Americans will be subject to the individual mandate penalty of $695 annually if they do not purchase federally-dictated health insurance ,\\\" the lawmakers wrote. \\\" However, under the new federal law, illegal immigrants will not be forced to purchase health insurance, though they will still be able to receive health care — regardless of their <cover>ability to pay — in a hospital's emergency department.\" Undocumented </cover>immigrants already have access to emergency-room treatment. \"So illegal immigrants get health care without paying for it, but citizens face the choice of either buying expensive health insurance or paying a tax,\" Coburn and Barrasso wrote. \" The cost of illegal immigrants‘ health care in the emergency department of hospitals will be shifted to Americans with insurance.\" Cite this Article Format mla apa chicago Your Citation Murse, Tom. \" Is Medical Help for Illegal Immigrants Covered Under Obamacare?\" ThoughtCo, Aug. 26, 2020, thoughtco.com/does-obamacare-cover-illegal-immigrants-3367966. Murse, Tom. ( 2020, August 26).\""}}
{"request":{"judgments":"26/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_410409857#7_918101125","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to whether illegal/undocumented immigrants receive medical help under Obamacare and directly states they are not covered through ACA insurance requirements but already have access to hospital emergency-room treatment regardless of ability to pay.","learned":"Undocumented immigrants generally are not covered by ACA insurance provisions, but hospitals must provide emergency department care regardless of ability to pay; uncompensated emergency costs may be shifted to others."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1371","reason":"This emergency-room/EMTALA query is focused on a key exception to general ineligibility and may retrieve additional direct sources on required emergency care regardless of immigration status or ability to pay."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1371"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_410409857#6_918099229","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1371","rank":2,"snippet":"health care reform law, criticized the Obama administration’s handling of illegal immigrants in a report titled \"Bad Medicine.\" They said the cost of allowing illegal immigrants to get health care in emergency rooms will cost taxpayers untold millions. \"Starting in 2014, Americans will be subject to the individual mandate penalty of $695 annually if they do not purchase federally-dictated health insurance ,\" the lawmakers wrote. \" However, under the new federal law, illegal immigrants will not be forced to purchase health insurance, though they will still be able to receive health care — regardless of their <cover>ability to pay — in a hospital's emergency department.\" Undocumented </cover>immigrants already have access to emergency-room treatment. \"So illegal immigrants get health care without paying for it, but citizens face the choice of either buying expensive health insurance or paying a tax,\" Coburn and Barrasso wrote. \" The cost of illegal immigrants‘ health care in the emergency department of hospitals will be shifted to Americans with insurance.\"\" , \"start_char\": 4895.000000 , \"title\": \"Is Medical Help for Illegal Immigrants Covered Under Obamacare?\" , \"url\": \"https://www.thoughtco.com/does-"}}
