{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_410409857#6_918099229","relevance":3,"reason":"This is a duplicate/near-duplicate segment from a document dedicated to whether illegal immigrants receive medical help under Obamacare. It directly states they are not required/covered under ACA insurance provisions but can receive hospital emergency-department care regardless of ability to pay.","learned":"Duplicate evidence: undocumented immigrants do not get broad ACA coverage, but emergency-room care is available regardless of ability to pay."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\") (+ \"state-funded\" \"state funds\" \"state-only\") (+ health coverage medicaid) (+ children adults))","reason":"Search for direct evidence on state-funded exceptions, since several strong sources note that some states provide Medicaid-like or other health coverage to certain undocumented immigrants despite federal restrictions."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\") (+ \"state-funded\" \"state funds\" \"state-only\") (+ health coverage medicaid) (+ children adults))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_42_554368983#3_1077505606","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1372","rank":1,"snippet":"Cal Rules implemented to limit California Medicaid estate recovery Who is eligible for Medicaid in California? How does Medicaid provide financial assistance to Medicare beneficiaries in California? How do I enroll in Medicaid in California? Medicaid expansion has played a key role in reducing the uninsured rate Funding for Medi-Cal California Medicaid History Apply for Medicaid in California Apply online California section \" , \"segment\": \"The Trump administration won a Supreme Court case on “public charge, ” which effectively discourages legal immigrants from using public assistance, including <cover>Medicaid. However, California is using state funds to cover undocumented immigrants under Medi-Cal, so undocumented young adults </cover>are not receiving a federally funded benefit (Medicaid is jointly funded by the state and federal government, but states can opt to add services or eligibility categories that are fully funded by the state). California had previously considered allowing undocumented immigrants to enroll in full-price private plans through Covered California (the state’s health insurance exchange), but that has not come to pass. SB10, which passed during the 2016 legislative session, initially called for allowing adults age 19 and over to enroll in Medi-Cal without regard for immigration status. "}}
