{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1529612638#0_3106534947","relevance":2,"reason":"The result is an explainer on how immigrants obtain health insurance under the ACA and includes a section titled 'Can Undocumented Immigrants Obtain Coverage?', but the snippet shows only headings and does not provide the actual answer.","learned":"A direct Q&A-style ACA immigrant health insurance article may contain a focused answer on undocumented immigrants' coverage options."},"action":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1529612638#0_3106534947","reason":"The snippet is promising but lacks the answer; retrieve the full document to confirm whether it directly explains undocumented immigrants' access to health insurance, Medicaid, and subsidies."}}
{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1529612638#0_3106534947"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1529612638#0_3106534947","document":"How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? ... How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? Some Different Rules Apply for Medicaid and for Premium Subsidies Are ACA Premium Subsidies Limited to U.S. Citizens? How Does the Exchange Know That Applicants Are Lawfully Present? What Coverage Is Available for Immigrants Who Are 65 or Older? Can an Immigrant Enroll in Coverage Outside of Open Enrollment? Can Undocumented Immigrants Obtain Coverage?  ... How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? Health Insurance Affordable Care Act & Obamacare How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? Some Different Rules Apply for Medicaid and for Premium Subsidies By Louise Norris twitter linkedin Louise Norris has been a licensed health insurance agent since 2003 after graduating magna cum laude from Colorado State with a BS in psychology. Learn about our editorial process Louise Norris Fact checked by Fact checked by Ashley Hall on March 14, 2020 linkedin Ashley Hall is a writer and fact checker who has been published in multiple medical journals in the field of surgery. Learn about our editorial process Ashley Hall Updated on October 21, 2020 If you're an immigrant arriving in the U.S., one of the first things on your to-do list is obtaining health insurance. Unlike many other countries, the U.S. does not have universal health coverage, and although Medicare and Medicaid are government-sponsored health plans, they're not available to new immigrants. So let's take a look at some frequently asked questions about what's available for immigrants, including new arrivals and those who have been in the U.S. for a long time. GCShutter / istockphoto / Getty Images Are ACA Premium Subsidies Limited to U.S. Citizens? No. Premium subsidies (premium tax credits) in the exchanges are available to lawfully-present residents, which includes a long list of immigration statuses (note that Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals—DACA—is not considered an eligible immigration status for purchasing coverage in the exchange).","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"37/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1529612638#0_3106534947","relevance":2,"reason":"The full document is an immigrant health insurance ACA explainer and indicates that Medicaid/Medicare are not generally available to new immigrants and that ACA subsidies are for lawfully present residents, with DACA not eligible. However, the returned document text does not include the actual 'Can Undocumented Immigrants Obtain Coverage?' answer section, so it is incomplete as direct evidence.","learned":"ACA health insurance and subsidies are described as available to lawfully present immigrants, not undocumented immigrants; the source likely has a direct undocumented-coverage section but it was not visible in the returned text."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1378","reason":"The direct question-style query is promising; continue to find snippets that include the explicit answer about undocumented immigrants' health insurance and Medicaid access."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1378"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1529612638#6_3106551014","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1378","rank":2,"snippet":"7438.000000 , \"headings\": \"How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? How Do Immigrants Obtain Health Insurance Under the ACA? Some Different Rules Apply for Medicaid and for Premium Subsidies Are ACA Premium Subsidies Limited to U.S. Citizens? How Does the Exchange Know That Applicants Are Lawfully Present? What Coverage Is Available for Immigrants Who Are 65 or Older? Can an Immigrant Enroll in Coverage Outside of Open Enrollment?<cover>Can Undocumented Immigrants Obtain Coverage? \" , \"segment\": \"Before 2014, there were few options for recent immigrants aged 65 or older. Private individual health insurance policies generally weren't available for anyone over the age of 64, and like Medicaid, </cover>there's a five-year wait before recent immigrants can enroll in Medicare. So older immigrants often had to rely on long-term travel insurance, unless they had access to an employer-sponsored plan in the U.S. Even after five years, Medicare was often unaffordable for immigrants. Since Medicare is partially funded by payroll taxes that U.S. workers pay during their careers, Medicare Part A (hospital insurance) is only premium-free for people who have paid "}}
