{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_1529612638#5_3106548719","relevance":2,"reason":"This segment from an ACA immigrant health insurance explainer is relevant because it explains that Marketplace coverage can be terminated if immigration documentation is not provided, but it still does not directly answer whether undocumented immigrants can obtain coverage or free healthcare.","learned":"Marketplace coverage requires proof of eligible immigration status; failure to provide immigration documentation can lead to coverage termination."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"illegals get it all for free\" \"free health care\" \"free healthcare\") (+ factcheck \"fact check\" reuters politifact snopes) (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\"))","reason":"Search for fact-checks and direct claim evaluations about undocumented or illegal immigrants allegedly getting free healthcare, which are likely to be dedicated to the exact information need."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"illegals get it all for free\" \"free health care\" \"free healthcare\") (+ factcheck \"fact check\" reuters politifact snopes) (+ undocumented \"illegal immigrants\"))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_479997533#5_985532663","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1379","rank":1,"snippet":"supplemental insurance while ‘illegals get it all for free’ Partly false claim: Seniors must pay for Medicare and supplemental insurance while ‘illegals get it all for free’ VERDICT \" , \"segment\": \"These include legal restrictions, inability to afford private insurance, and not seeking other options due to fear of deportation ( here ). The KFF reports that 47% of undocumented immigrants are uninsured. The think tank Public Policy Institute of California (PPIC) says the number is 60% to 70%. Undocumented immigrants are excluded from government marketplaces like Medicare and ACA. Only emergency treatment is required to be administered to people regardless of their immigration status. VERDICT Partly false: Seniors on Social Security must pay for Medicare and supplemental insurance, but undocumented immigrants do not get the same health insurance coverage, or health care, for free Our Standards: The Thomson Reuters Trust Principles.\" , \"start_char\": 3207.000000 , \"title\": \"Partly false claim: Seniors must pay for Medicare and supplemental insurance while ‘<cover>illegals get it all for free’ | Reuters\" , \"url\": \"https://www.reuters.com/article/uk-factcheck-undocumented-</cover>free-healthcar-idUSKBN20Y3FD\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"39/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_479997533#5_985532663","relevance":3,"reason":"The Reuters fact-check is dedicated to the exact claim that 'illegals get it all for free' and directly concludes the claim is partly false: undocumented immigrants do not get the same health insurance coverage or health care for free, are excluded from Medicare/ACA marketplaces, and only emergency treatment is required regardless of status.","learned":"Direct Reuters verdict: undocumented immigrants do not receive the same health insurance coverage or health care for free; emergency treatment is the main required exception, and many remain uninsured."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1379","reason":"This direct fact-check query is highly aligned with the exact information need and may surface additional claim-checking or explanatory documents."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1379"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_479997533#0_985523054","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1379","rank":2,"snippet":"while ‘illegals get it all for free’ By Reuters Staff 5 Min Read A viral image on social media asks why seniors have to pay for Medicare and Supplement Insurance while “illegals get it all for free.” The post from January 27, 2019 has over 37,000 shares as of March 5, 2020 ( here ). The claim is false. Seniors on Social Security must pay for Medicare and supplemental insurance, but undocumented immigrants do not get the same health insurance coverage, or health care, for free. The U.S. federal health insurance program for senior citizens is made up of different parts. Medicare Part A (hospital Insurance) can sometimes be free, but only for some seniors. Medicare Part B (medical insurance) has a monthly premium. The Medicare Advantage Plan (formerly known as Part C) and Medicare Part D (prescription drug coverage) also have monthly premiums.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Partly false claim: Seniors must pay for Medicare and supplemental insurance while ‘<cover>illegals get it all for free’ | Reuters\" , \"url\": \"https://www.reuters.com/article/uk-factcheck-undocumented-</cover>free-healthcar-idUSKBN20Y3FD\" }"}}
