{"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1227247183#0_2452892131"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_52_1227247183#0_2452892131","document":"Do Seniors on Social Security Have to Pay for Medicare While 'Illegal Immigrants' Get It Free? | Snopes.com ... Do Seniors on Social Security Have to Pay for Medicare While ‘Illegal Immigrants’ Get It Free? Do Seniors on Social Security Have to Pay for Medicare While ‘Illegal Immigrants’ Get It Free? It's a familiar trope on the internet but remains factually challenged. Claim Rating Origin Keep Snopes Debunking Editors' Picks What Is Critical Race Theory and Why Are Some People So Mad at It? We talked to experts who have the answers. Under HIPAA Rules, Can Businesses Ask If You Have Been Vaccinated Against COVID-19? Where does HIPAA's privacy rule apply?  ... Do Seniors on Social Security Have to Pay for Medicare While 'Illegal Immigrants' Get It Free? | Snopes.com Home Fact Checks Politics Do Seniors on Social Security Have to Pay for Medicare While ‘Illegal Immigrants’ Get It Free? Do Seniors on Social Security Have to Pay for Medicare While ‘Illegal Immigrants’ Get It Free? It's a familiar trope on the internet but remains factually challenged. Bethania Palma Published 19 June 2019 Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on Pinterest Share on Reddit Share via Email Image via John Ewing/Portland Press Herald / Getty Images Claim Senior Citizens on Social Security in the U.S. have to pay for Medicare while \\\"illegal immigrants\\\" get it for free. Rating False About this rating Subscribe to our Snopes Debunker newsletter and get the latest fact checks in your inbox for free: By subscribing, you're accepting our terms and conditions and privacy policy. Keep reading, our fact check continues below. Origin In May and June 2019, a misleading but widely seen meme about immigrants and Medicare benefits continued to circulate on Facebook: Although the trope that undocumented immigrants are cashing in on U.S. government-funded public benefits for free is a common one, it’s generally misleading.","ok":true,"op":"document"}}
